  "best_arm_at_threshold": "R5_tabular",
  "caveat": "Net benefit reads the PROBABILITY SCALE; AUROC reads only the ranking. An arm that ranks well can still lose at a fixed threshold because its probabilities are inflated, and that is a finding about the probability scale rather than about discrimination. R6_waveform and R7_waveform_demo_acq were fitted under focal BCE at gamma 2 (D-049) and their reported score is a mean over four crops (D-050) and then over five seeds (D-055). D-065 stated this before any of these numbers existed, and recalibration was declared out of scope in the same entry because only test-fold predictions are stored and refitting on them is circular. No net-benefit result may be read as evidence about discrimination, and no claim in the abstract rests on one.",
  "what_this_does_not_decide": "Nothing here changes any pre-declared outcome. All three quantitative targets failed at the endpoints they named (D-036, D-062, D-063) and the horizon-ladder trend is unsupported (D-062). Calibration and net benefit are strengtheners 9 and 10 in PLAN.md section 4, cut first if the schedule slips, and the confirmatory set depends on neither."
